.TH SDL_GetGamepadJoystick 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetGamepadJoystick \- Get the underlying joystick from a gamepad.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_gamepad.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_Joystick * SDL_GetGamepadJoystick(SDL_Gamepad *gamepad);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This function will give you a
.BR SDL_Joystick
object, which allows you to use the
.BR SDL_Joystick
functions with a
.BR SDL_Gamepad
object\[char46] This would be useful for getting a joystick\(aqs position at any given time, even if it hasn\(aqt moved (moving it would produce an event, which would have the axis\(aq value)\[char46]
.PP
The pointer returned is owned by the
.BR SDL_Gamepad \[char46]
You should not call
.BR SDL_CloseJoystick ()
on it, for example, since doing so will likely cause SDL to crash\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I gamepad
the gamepad object that you want to get a joystick from\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns an
.BR SDL_Joystick
object, or NULL on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

